gh drawdown in 2027-36) = 0.81, uncontested across all five panelists (9 of 10 decade windows since 1970; AI-Q4 at 76-80% already posits the trigger; USD denomination and a price rather than total-return basis each make 25% easier; the IMF's explicit 20% AI-led valuation shock).\nSub-step 2, P(no-rally type | a drawdown occurs). The Reference-Class panelist's regime-sorting is the correct frame and his own evidence supports a higher conditional than he used: all five fails (1973-74, 1980-81, 1987, 1990, 2022) sit in inflation-salient regimes and all three passes (2000-02, 2007-09, 2020) in 1998-2021, yet he assigned the inflation-salient regime only ~30% weight while his own CQ2 OECD-core marginal implied more. With my regime weight of 0.38 (see the coherence check below): 0.38(0.80) + 0.62(0.22) = 0.304 + 0.136 = 0.44. Add +0.05 for the Auditor's index-construction point, which both Wave-2 panelists correctly rescued: under the Section-locked PPP weights Japan is ~12-13% at a yield floor that cannot contribute 50bp of rally and Italy ~6-7% with spreads that WIDEN in risk-off, so the remaining ~0.81 of the aggregate must fall ~65bp for the aggregate to fall 50bp. Conditional = 0.49, with little compounding across multiple episodes because the regime is common within a decade. B = 0.81 x 0.49 = 0.40.\nCORRELATION. Strongly positive, rho ~ +0.58: a high-bp-vol decade is definitionally the regime in which the equity-bond hedge fails, and in my CQ4 decomposition the same +80bp term-premium term generates both. P(A|B) = 0.70.\nJOINT = 0.40 x 0.70 = 0.28 -> 30 after a small upward adjustment for the fact that my CQ4 P90 branch and my CQ6-C mass both sit inside the qualifying regime. ANSWER 30. This is my largest single move off the Wave-1 modal (24-28), and it is a half-move toward the red-team: I take his mechanism and reject his calibration on the one piece of realized data that bears on it.\nCOHERENCE CHECK WITH CQ6 (required by my lens). The inflation-salient regime w