e US 10-year nominal Treasury yield averaged at or above 4.25% over the same five years (i.e. the floor does NOT shift with the yield level).\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies the bp-normalization argument on which my half-move toward the red-team rests. CQ5's conjunct A falls from 0.48 to ~0.30 and CQ5 from 30 to ~20, i.e. back onto the Wave-1 centre; my CQ4 +80bp term-premium term weakens and P90 falls from 3.3 to ~3.0; CQ6-C loses ~3pp to B. Conversely a trailing five-year average above 115 with the same yields takes CQ5 to ~40 and vindicates the red-team.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Eurostat SES 2030 wave (published ~2032-33) plus US BLS OES show cumulative real median gross hourly earnings growth for NACE/ISIC F+Q exceeding J+K+M by more than +6.0pp over the 2022-2030 interval, with a published decomposition showing within-job wage growth rather than composition dominating.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2033\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies my -6.0pp composition wedge (it would imply nearer -2pp) and with it the central reason CQ1 sits at 16. CQ1's second conjunct rises from 0.22 to ~0.42 and CQ1 from 16 to ~26, vindicating the red-team's dilution-contradiction attack at full strength; hypothesis (a) rises from 4 to ~10; CQ6 shifts ~4pp from D into B. A gap below +1.0pp, or negative, takes CQ1 to ~9 and plank (a) to 2.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"OECD International Migration Outlook reports combined annual OECD-38 entries of foreign-trained nurses, aides and personal-care workers above 1.0M/yr in any single year, with mean time-to-licensure for an India- or Philippines-trained nurse below 12 months in at least three of the US, Germany, Japan, Canada and the UK.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2033\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies the 400-700k/yr administrative throughput cap that both my dilution arithmetic and my Baumol drag depend on, and does so in a way that cuts BOTH my CQ1 legs: the care constraint then clears on migration rather than on wa